# Shell scripts and systemd units must always check out with LF line
# endings, regardless of the cloning machine's core.autocrlf setting --
# a CRLF shebang line ("#!/usr/bin/env bash\r") fails on Linux with
# "bad interpreter: ... no such file or directory". These are deployed to
# and run on Linux targets even when authored/committed from Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/*.service text eol=lf
